      "latency_ms": 25342.0,
      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1148,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical substance with the chemical formula **H₂O**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what makes water unique and important:\n\n### 1. The Chemical Structure\nWater is a **polar molecule**. Because oxygen is more \"thirsty\" for electrons than hydrogen, the oxygen end of the molecule has a slight negative charge, and the hydrogen ends have a slight positive charge. This polarity allows water to stick to itself (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion), making it an excellent solvent.\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is unique because it is the only common substance found naturally on Earth that can exist as a **solid, liquid, and gas** at temperatures commonly found on the planet.\n*   **Liquid:** This is the state we use for drinking, washing, and swimming.\n*   **Solid (Ice):** When water freezes, the molecules lock into a rigid crystal structure. Interestingly, water is one of the very few substances where the solid form is less dense than the liquid form. This is why ice floats on water, which is essential for aquatic life (it insulates the water below).\n*   **Gas (Steam/Water Vapor):** When water is heated, it turns into a gas that rises into the atmosphere.\n\n### 3. Key Properties\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is the main component of blood, sap, and ocean water, and why it is necessary for chemical reactions in the body.\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick together very strongly at the surface, creating a kind of \"skin.\" This allows small insects to walk across puddles without sinking.\n*   **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before it gets hot, and it releases a lot of heat before it freezes. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps our bodies at a stable temperature.\n\n### 4. Importance to Life\nWater is the foundation of life as we know it. It is the primary component of all living cells (roughly 60% of the human body is water). It is used for:\n*   Transporting nutrients and oxygen to cells.\n*   Removing waste products.\n*   Lubricating joints.\n*   Regulating body temperature through sweating and panting."
    },
